In the early implementation of the time schedule for the construction or reconstruction of stadiums, streets, hotels and airports, both hosts are lagging.
It's even possible that the number of stadiums for ME will decrease from eight to six.
"We can't waste any more time.
We have to work as quickly as possible now," said Grigory Surkis, the chairman of the Ukrainian union.
"UEFA will keep an eye on us."
An even more radical move has been agreed in Poland.
The leadership of Poland's PZPN union has been dismissed after numerous scandals by the National Olympic Committee and replaced by independent administrator Robert Zawlocki.
The committee met at the request of Sports Minister Mirosław Drzewiecki.
“There is a “serious danger that PZPN won’t be able to act according to the rules,” Drzewiecki told Polish news agency PAP.
"We have assured UEFA President Michel Platini by letter that preparations for the 2012 European Championships will not suffer through this step."
Several teams from the Premier League were doomed only last season because of manipulations, and in the end he had to move the start of the league quickly.
