BSkyB lost litigation to review the decision of the Competition Commission, which ordered the firm to reduce its stake in competing broadcaster ITV.
BSkyB’s competition appeals tribunal has indicated it to reduce its ITV stake from 17,9 % below 7.5%.
Previously, the Commission claimed that BSkyB's share obstructed the competitive struggle and gave the company a disproportionate influence on ITV.
BSkyB bought a stake in 2006 in a deal that, as a result, prevented NTL, now renamed Virgin Media, to buy ITV.
